    "created_at": "2020-04-30T19:14:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-30T19:14:51Z",
    "body": "@xfq In https://github.com/w3c/i18n-drafts/issues/123 you noted that links don't have this problem. What's different about links vs summary that makes one a problem and the other not? And could that difference be implemented in UAs, instead of making them unselectable?\r\n\r\n(Fwiw I agree with @domenic and @annevk that disabling selection isn't the right solution here, improving browser UX is.)",
